<item><title>Cameroon regulator flags CFAF18.6 billion in telecom violations</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-regulator-flags-cfaf18-6-billion-in-telecom-e777a4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-regulator-flags-cfaf18-6-billion-in-telecom-e777a4/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>ART identified 93 violations involving CAMTEL, Orange Cameroon and MTN Cameroon, with the state-owned CAMTEL accounting for the largest share.</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:20:06 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroon ships first 17 tons of coffee to China duty-free</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-ships-first-17-tons-of-coffee-to-china-duty-free-bfb842/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-ships-first-17-tons-of-coffee-to-china-duty-free-bfb842/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The Ministry of Finance says the shipment qualifies under Beijing&apos;s zero-tariff policy, which gives Cameroonian exporters duty-free entry to the Chinese market.</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:01:43 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
